{"id": "EUVD-2026-105212", "enisaUuid": "d3db1d3e-4507-3e04-bb36-e860b2402f32", "description": "A vulnerability has been found in aaPanel up to 8.25.0. The affected element is the function ExecShell of the file class/public/common.py of the component File Manager. The manipulation of the argument sfile/dfile/access/user leads to os command injection. The attack is possible to be carried out remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The vendor confirms: \"The reported RCE and LFI vulnerabilities require authentication.\"", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T17:15:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T19:05:49", "baseScore": 9.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H/E:P", "references": ["https://vuldb.com/vuln/422748", "https://vuldb.com/vuln/422748/cti", "https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-113506", "https://vuldb.com/submit/996819", "https://github.com/JdExploit/aapanel-cve-2026/tree/master/aapanel-rce"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xjfc-j86g-w62p", "CVE-2026-113506"], "assigner": "VulDB", "epss": 2.08, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00033263-d9f5-3225-9b56-8d07d11ed058", "product": {"name": "aaPanel", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "8.24"}, {"id": "0477cec7-fb71-31cb-b306-26ef7508749e", "product": {"name": "aaPanel", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "8.9"}, {"id": "129daa43-61f7-373c-9327-a4a78ae0bb92", "product": {"name": "aaPanel", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "8.3"}, {"id": "2bef8368-6a10-33ec-a8ed-1d2fa9716157", "product": {"name": "aaPanel", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "8.23"}, {"id": "7b4ff6db-751f-3413-ba6b-939a8d198987", "product": {"name": "aaPanel", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "8.20"}, {"id": "7cce57db-bf26-3b3a-92b3-44487d571695", "product": {"name": "aaPanel", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "8.15"}, {"id": "7e7c82ca-6fa2-320f-86fa-159adbb8346a", "product": {"name": "aaPanel", "vend